			"color":"#322",
			"widgets_values":[
				"Create a 10-second, 9:16 vertical Apple-style minimalist product film for a pair of silver over-ear wireless headphones with off-white cushioned ear pads. Use the three anchor photos below as visual references: Photo 1 is the hero 3/4 back-angle product shot on a clean white background; Photo 2 is a close-up of the soft ear-pad texture and brushed-metal hinge; Photo 3 is the final composition showing the full headphone with the single-line English copy \"Hear the Quiet.\" in SF Pro Display Semibold, first half dark gray and second half silver-white.\n\n[Shot 1] Live-action, cinematic, white-tech minimalist, the silver headphones sit in a clean white negative-space environment, shown from a 3/4 back angle. A thin highlight slides along the metal edge of the headband. The camera pushes in with small amplitude at slow speed while the right ear cup rotates outward slightly.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:01.500, the camera cuts to a front-facing medium shot. Soft blurred visual noise waves (suggesting city/traffic sound) drift toward the headphones from the background. The ear cups remain still, then the inner ring of each ear cup glows subtly.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:03.000, the camera cuts to a close-up of the right ear cup as the cushion appears to gently compress inward, and the approaching noise waves dissipate around the ear cup, implying active noise cancellation. The motion is quick and decisive.\n\n[Shot 4] At 00:05.000, the shot cuts to an extreme close-up of the off-white ear-pad texture and the brushed-metal hinge. The camera holds a static shot while soft light moves slowly across the materials.\n\n[Shot 5] At 00:07.000, the camera cuts back to the 3/4 front hero view on the clean white background. The first half of the English copy \"Hear the\" appears in dark gray, centered in the upper-middle negative space. At 00:08.000, the second half \"Quiet.\" appears in silver-white next to it, and the first half shifts slightly within the same line to make room. The headphones remain stable.\n\n[Shot 6] At 00:09.000, the full single-line copy \"Hear the Quiet.\" stays on screen with the headphones until the video ends.\n\noverall_soundscape: A faint city rumble and distant traffic gradually approach, then suddenly collapse into silence; a soft, tactile ear-pad compression sound and a subtle electronic activation tone mark the noise-cancellation moment.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: Sparse tech plucks and airy pads at around 100 BPM, with a soft sub-bass drop synchronized to the noise-cancellation beat, ending on a clean single note.\n"
			],
